[h1]War Sliders[/h1]

The game's automation raises army, navy and fort maintenance when a war starts, but never lowers them afterwards. Auto-minting holds inflation where it is and never works off what the war added. After every small war you end up doing the same clicks by hand. This mod does them for you.

[b]What it does[/b]
[list]
[*] [b]Maintenance:[/b] puts the army, navy and fort sliders back to the peacetime value you choose. Never below the game's own minimum.
[*] [b]Inflation:[/b] if inflation is above your target, switches auto-minting off, sets minting each month by the game's own forecast until inflation reaches the target, then switches auto-minting back on.
[/list]

[b]When it runs[/b]
[list]
[*] By itself, once, the day after a war or a revolt ends, if no other war is left. Can be switched off.
[*] By a button on the Community Mod Framework quick-button panel, or on the mod's page in the CMF menu.
[/list]
Between wars it does nothing at all: no daily or monthly checks.

[b]Settings[/b] (mod page in the CMF menu)
Which sliders to lower and to what value, whether to work off inflation, the inflation target, and how low minting may go while working it off. An optional diagnostics window shows what the mod is doing.

[b]Requires[/b]
Community Mod Framework.

[b]Compatible[/b]
Changes no game files, only adds its own; works alongside interface mods.

[b]Localization[/b]
English, Русский

[i]The mod and this description were created with the help of an AI. It has been tested as far as was possible.[/i]
